meta {
  name: BookController
  seq: 1
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Roles accepted, per access rules §3:

    GET     /books, /books/search, /books/{id}      any signed-in user
    GET     /books/{id}/copies, /books/key-stages   any signed-in user
    POST    /books                                  librarian, admin
    PUT     /books/{id}                             librarian, admin
    DELETE  /books/{id}                             admin only

  `deleteBook` is the one line of this folder a librarian is refused. A book record is
  shared by every library and its copies cascade with it, so one deletion can empty
  another library's shelves — no per-library scope could make it safe (access rules
  §4.1). A librarian sending it gets 403; an administrator gets 204, or 409 when a copy
  has ever been borrowed.
}
